<title>GABON: GOVERNMENT LIST.</title>
<headline>GOVERNMENT LIST.</headline>
<text>
<p>GABON GOVERNMENT LIST (970128)</p>
<p>  **********************************************************</p>
<p>  * 28 Jan 97 - President Omar Bongo asked Paulin Obame-   *</p>
<p>  *		 Nguema to form a new government, three days*</p>
<p>  *		 after his old cabinet had offered its	*</p>
<p>  *		 resignation.					 *</p>
<p>  **********************************************************</p>
<p>			     - - - - - - -</p>
<p> President............Omar BONGO</p>
<p>(Sworn in 22 Jan 94 for a fifth five-year term)</p>
<p>			     - - - - - - -</p>
<p>GOVERNMENT (Formed 30 Oct 94, tendered resignation 24 Jan 97)</p>
<p> Prime Minister.............Paulin OBAME-NGUEMA</p>
<p>(Appointed 12 Oct 94, sworn in 2 Nov 94)</p>
<p>			     - - - - - - -</p>
<p>MINISTERS OF STATE:</p>
<p> Agriculture &amp; Rural Development.........Emmanuel ONDO METOGHO</p>
<p>Communication, Culture, Arts, Popular</p>
<p>    Education, Human Rights.......Sebastien MAMBOUNDOU MOUYAMA</p>
<p> Equipment &amp; Construction.......Zacharie MYBOTO</p>
<p>Foreign Affairs &amp; Cooperation..Casimir OYE MBA</p>
<p>Housing, Urban Development, Relations with</p>
<p>Parliament....Jean-Francois NTOUTOUME EMANE</p>
<p> Justice ............Max REMONDO</p>
<p>Labour, Human Resources, Professional</p>
<p>    Training............Jean Remy PENDI BOUYIKI</p>
<p>			     - - - - - - -</p>
<p>MINISTERS:</p>
<p> Defence, Security, Immigration...........General Idriss NGARI</p>
<p>Education, Youth, Sports, Women's issues....Paulette MISSAMBO</p>
<p> Finance &amp; Budget........Marcel DOUPAMBI MATOKA</p>
<p> Health and Population.........Serge MBA BEKALE</p>
<p>Higher Education &amp; Scientific Research...Gaston MOZOGHO OVONO</p>
<p>Interior....Louis-Gaston MAYILA</p>
<p> Mines, Energy &amp; Oil...............Paul TOUNGUI</p>
<p>Planning.....Senturel MADOUNGOU</p>
<p> Public Service &amp; Administrative Reform........Alexandre SAMBA</p>
<p>Social Affairs, National</p>
<p>    Solidarity................Simon OYONO ABA'A</p>
<p>Trade &amp; Industry, Small &amp; Medium-Sized Businesses,</p>
<p>Restructuring of the para-public sector,</p>
<p>    privatisation.........Andre Dieudonne BERRE</p>
<p>Transport, Merchant Navy, Fishing, Tourism,</p>
<p>National Parks.....Antoine MBOUMBOU MIYAKOU</p>
<p>Water &amp; Forestry, Posts &amp; Telecommunications,</p>
<p>    Environment...........Martin Fidele MAGNAGA</p>
<p>			     - - - - - - -</p>
<p>Central Bank Governor.....Jean-Felix MAMALEPOT</p>
<p>(Central Bank of Central African States)</p>
<p>Central Bank Director....Jean-Paul LEYIMANGOYE</p>
<p>			     - - - - - - -</p>
<p>	 NOTE: Any comments/queries on the content of this</p>
<p>		 government list, please contact the Reuter</p>
<p>		 Editorial Reference Unit, London, on (171) 542</p>
<p>		 7968.</p>
<p>			  (End government list)</p>
</text>
